  "comment": "**What it does**\nQuality compounders among banks and insurers, judged by THEIR rules rather than the ones that don't apply to financials.\n- **Your choices:** ROE 12%+ without extreme leverage doing the work, book value growing 7%+, reasonable price-to-book, above the 200-day line, decent RS Rank, $1B+.\n- Book-value growth is the right compounding measure here \u2014 retained earnings compound into book value, which is how financials actually grow.\n- 'Reasonable OR below peers' is a real either/or: P/B at or under 2.5, or below its industry median. Negative-book-value names are excluded from the peer test rather than appearing as a deep discount.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- Widen it: drop `roe` from 12 to 10, or book-value growth from 7% to 5%.\n- Cheaper only: drop the `pb` ceiling from 2.5 to 1.5.\n- The bank+insurance universe is small (~773 rows), so counts stay modest.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- Sort by `quality_score`, tiebreak `momentum_score`.\n- Avoid sorting by `value_score` (P/B is already in the filter) and `income_score` (dividends are out of scope for this screen).\n\n_Built 2026-08-13 \u00b7 65 matches at build time._",
  "ai_instructions": "Find quality compounders among banks and insurers \u2014 the group my\nquality_compounders screen excludes on purpose, judged by THEIR rules: return on\nequity and growing book value, not margins and current ratios.\n- **Goal**: long-term growth in financials. **Kinds**: banks and insurance only.\n- **Quality, their way**: ROE 12%+ (without crazy leverage doing the work).\n- **Compounding, their way**: book value growing ~7%+ a year (earnings retained\n  into book is how financials compound); forward earnings growth as a fallback.\n- **Not overpriced**: price-to-book reasonable or below industry peers.\n- **Proven**: above the 200-day line, decent RS Rank.\n- **Dividends**: ignore for this screen. **Size**: $1B and bigger. **Risk**: moderate.\n- **Results**: ~20-150 names. **Sorting**: quality first, tiebreak momentum.",
